      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "for performance and validation reasons i say no as well as someone who uses the interface and who has done work this before this would really muck up the work flow and if your testing a DEVELOPMENT build you should put it on a SEPORATE Build ID. I fail to see the issue here other than user error. keep build ids separate and you should be fine and if that's still the issue just copy and rebuild the map in a new scene or project. if your uploading in a collab there should only be one uploader going through idk google drive plus if multiple people try uploading a file at the same time it might corrupt the map thus ruining your work until next upload also it leaves corrupted data on an already unstable server.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-01-23T20:39:25.690Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When working with collaborators, it's common for multiple project members to have their own builds of a world for in-game testing.  It is not always obvious if you were not the last one to upload, and the current process will fail AFTER the lengthy build process if the account does not own the blueprint.\nI suggest greying out the Build & Publish button (or putting in the account check and fail before the scene build) so that the build time is not wasted.",
